Dear all,

ever since this paper <https://academic.oup.com/auk/article/125/2/336/5148162?login=true> I have known that in principle we can separate the effects of a covariate on the state and the observation parts of a hierarchical model (and surely other people have shown this before ---- there is rarely something new under the sun). I wouldn’t be surprised if there are situations where the model breaks when a single covariate has effects on both parts of the model, but I’d be interested to see someone identifying these conditions in a controlled simulation study.

As a small part in another modeling project <https://esajournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ecy.4292>, with what we call an integrated distance sampling model, we have just repeated such a type of simulation, where the same covariate affected both components of the model, and things worked just wonderfully (this is Simulation 2 in the paper).

Best regards  -- Marc

