Good evening Marc,

Thank you so much for your response.

I have used a 'stacked' dataset over 3 years with 110 sites each year
(2 visits each site). I use sites as a random effect in my models.
For this particular species, it was detected at only 24 visits.

My global model has two parameters for detection, and 4 for occupancy,
including my random effect (site).

Here is the output for one of the two models that I deem 'suspect' due
to the huge random effect variance:

Call:
occu(formula = ~1 ~ scale(build_100m) + (1 | site), data =
INBU_stat.sample.unmarkedFrame_cov)

Occupancy (logit-scale):
Random effects:
 Groups        Name Variance Std.Dev.
   site (Intercept) 4231.176   65.047

Fixed effects:
                   Estimate     SE       z  P(>|z|)
(Intercept)       -12.40749 2.5128 -4.9377 7.90e-07
scale(build_100m)  -0.00561 0.0652 -0.0861 9.31e-01

Detection (logit-scale):
 Estimate     SE     z  P(>|z|)
    -1.62 0.0961 -16.8 1.49e-63

AIC: 180.7833
Number of sites: 294
optim convergence code: 0
optim iterations: 68
Bootstrap iterations: 0

Compared to the output of a model which had much lower variance:

Call:
occu(formula = ~1 ~ scale(vl_100m) + scale(build_100m) + (1 |
    site), data = INBU_stat.sample.unmarkedFrame_cov)

Occupancy (logit-scale):
Random effects:
 Groups        Name Variance Std.Dev.
   site (Intercept)    0.048    0.218

Fixed effects:
                  Estimate    SE      z  P(>|z|)
(Intercept)        -1.9245 0.645 -2.983 0.002852
scale(vl_100m)      1.1628 0.342  3.403 0.000667
scale(build_100m)   0.0869 0.317  0.274 0.784328

Detection (logit-scale):
 Estimate    SE     z P(>|z|)
    -1.21 0.545 -2.23  0.0258

AIC: 190.5375
Number of sites: 294
optim convergence code: 0
optim iterations: 35
Bootstrap iterations: 0

In my original run, I simply excluded the two models with exceptionally
high variance in the random effect. The results of the mb.gof.test on
the global model turned out that c-hat of 0.35, which I assume I can
correct to c-hat = 1.

Thank you again for your time and support. It is much appreciated.

- Chris 🐦🌱

